### Scenario 5 - B2B customer (5): 200 EUR HT minimum, then payment on credit
### Customer 5: credit limit 5000, outstanding 2000 (available 3000)

@order = http://localhost:8083
@customer = http://localhost:8082

### Credit before
GET {{customer}}/customers/5/credit

### 1. Cart below the minimum (2 x ELC-3001 = 56.81 HT)
# @name cart
POST {{order}}/carts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": 5 }

###
POST {{order}}/carts/{{cart.response.body.id}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "ELC-3001", "qty": 2 }

### Refused: B2B orders require at least 200.00 EUR HT
POST {{order}}/carts/{{cart.response.body.id}}/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "shippingMethod": "STANDARD" }

### 2. Add a chair, checkout works: goodsHt = 369.36
POST {{order}}/carts/{{cart.response.body.id}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "HOM-4002", "qty": 1 }

###
# @name checkout
POST {{order}}/carts/{{cart.response.body.id}}/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "shippingMethod": "STANDARD" }

### 3. Points are forbidden for B2B
POST {{order}}/orders/{{checkout.response.body.id}}/pay
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "B2B_CREDIT", "loyaltyPoints": 100 }

### 4. Pay on credit (no loyalty points earned for B2B)
POST {{order}}/orders/{{checkout.response.body.id}}/pay
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "B2B_CREDIT" }

### Credit after: outstanding = 2000 + 443.23
GET {{customer}}/customers/5/credit

### B2B_CREDIT is refused for a B2C customer (try it on an order of customer 1)
# POST {{order}}/orders/<id>/pay   { "method": "B2B_CREDIT" }
